.SH TRANSFER SYNTAXES
The ASN.1 family of standards defines a number of ways to encode data,
including byte\-oriented (e.g., BER and CBOR), bit\-oriented (e.g.,
PER), and textual (e.g., XER and JER).
Some encoding variants (e.g., DER) are stricter variants of more general
encodings (e.g., BER).
.PP
